  <content>
  <section><section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="91b86a46-3b99-4625-ad43-24e8495050c2"><problem><para>
      <para>Functions \(a, b, c, d, e\), and \(f\) are given below. Which functions are linear? <emphasis>Select the three</emphasis> answers
          that apply.</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>["\\(a(x)=3x\\)", "\\(d(x)=9+3x\\)", "\\(f(x)=9 \\cdot 3x\\)"]</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(a(x)=3x\), \(d(x)=9+3x\), \( f(x)=9 \cdot 3x\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><para>Use the given information for problems 4 – 6. Technology is required. Function \(f\) is defined by \(f(x)=3x+5\),
  and function \(g\) is defined by \(g(x)=(1.1)^x\).</para>
<table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        \(f(x)\)
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        \(g(x)\)
      </emphasis></entry></row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        1
      </emphasis></entry><entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        5
      </emphasis></entry><entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        10
      </emphasis></entry><entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        20
      </emphasis></entry><entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="04eb6bed-b602-46eb-95d3-8bcd36a15239"><problem><para>
      <para>Which values will complete the table for \(f(x)\)?</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>8, 11, 14, 17</para><para>8, 20, 35, 65</para><para>3, 15, 30, 60</para><para>8, 15, 30, 60</para></problem><solution><para>8, 20, 35, 65</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 8, 20, 35, 65. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
